From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] ui-egui: tooltips of icon toggles, colour splits, galleries, swatches and shape tiles go through the catalog

Owner testing the MSI (ru, uz): most Slides toolbar and ribbon tooltips stayed English. The ribbon helpers already translated the label of tip(id, label), but the shared widget sinks (icon_toggle, color_split, the colour swatches, gallery tiles) and about a dozen tile hovers (shape presets, freeform tools, icon cells, warp tiles, table styles, selection pane buttons, thesaurus buttons, the corner-smoothing hint) passed their literal on as is. Each now wraps its text in crate::i18n::t (unknown text is returned unchanged, so English is untouched). Literal strings were already catalog rows; labels computed elsewhere (shape presets, icon names) translate only where the catalog has them.
---
 crates/ui-egui/src/panes.rs   |  4 ++--
 crates/ui-egui/src/ribbon.rs  | 14 +++++++-------
 crates/ui-egui/src/selpane.rs |  2 +-
 crates/ui-egui/src/widgets.rs |  6 ++++--
 4 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

